    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0231" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8982: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-05-28T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1927—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 28—7:52 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>United States Ship <hi rendition="#italic">Pigeon</hi> fired upon with machine
                    guns and shrapnel by Southern troops while passing Chenglingki above Hankow
                    yesterday afternoon en route to Ichang to evacuate Standard Oil Company stocks.
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Pigeon</hi> returned fire with machine guns and 14
                    rounds of shrapnel shells. Engagement lasted approximately fifteen minutes; no
                    casualties on <hi rendition="#italic">Pigeon</hi> although vessel struck number
                    of times by machine-gun bullets.</p>
                <p>Destroyer <hi rendition="#italic">Edsall</hi> left Hankow this morning to escort
                    United States Ship <hi rendition="#italic">Penguin</hi> by Chenglingki late
                    today or tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Legation informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
